  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The last day to file your 2025 federal income tax return is Wednesday, April 15, 2026. Electronic returns must be submitted by midnight in your time zone, and paper returns must be postmarked by this date. If you owe taxes, payment is also due on April 15, 2026, regardless of an extension.Key details regarding the 2026 filing deadline:Extensions: You can file Form 4868 by April 15 to get an automatic extension until October 15, 2026, to file your paperwork, but this does not delay payment obligations.Where to File: You can prepare and e-file your return using the IRS Free File program or H&R Block.Penalties: Late filing penalties can reach 5% of unpaid taxes per month, up to 25%.Support: Free assistance is available through VITA/TCE/AARP Tax-Aide sites.Important Dates: Information for crucial tax deadlines can be found at TurboTax.For those living outside the United States and Puerto Rico, the deadline to file is June 15, 2026.",
